    "The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 created the SEC and governs the secondary market (trading); the 1933 Act governs new issues.",
    "The SEC is the top regulator but is NOT an SRO; FINRA, MSRB, and exchanges are SROs under SEC oversight; the SEC never approves or guarantees securities.",
    "Broker = agent (commission, works for customer); dealer = principal (markup/markdown, trades from own inventory). A firm can't be both on the same trade.",
    "A market maker is always a principal; it quotes a bid (buys) and an ask (sells) and profits from the spread.",
    "NYSE = auction market with ONE Designated Market Maker (DMM) per stock; Nasdaq/OTC = negotiated market with MANY competing market makers.",
    "Most bonds — government, corporate, and municipal — trade OTC, not on an exchange.",
    "ATS is the broad SEC category (Reg ATS); ECNs and dark pools are types of ATS.",
    "Dark pool = no pre-trade transparency (hidden orders, anonymous blocks); ECN = automated order matching, displayed quotes, after-hours trading.",
    "First market = listed traded ON an exchange; Second = unlisted/OTC; Third = listed traded OTC; Fourth = institution-to-institution direct via ECN (no broker-dealer).",
    "Bid = customer sells; Ask/offer = customer buys; Spread = Ask − Bid; narrow spread = liquid, wide spread = illiquid.",
    "Market order = guarantees execution, not price; limit order = guarantees price (or better), not execution.",
    "Buy limit fills at the limit price or lower; sell limit fills at the limit price or higher.",
    "Regular-way settlement is T+1 for stocks and corporate/municipal bonds (effective May 28, 2024), regardless of trading venue.",
    "Issuer registration and prospectus = 1933 Act; broker-dealer/exchange registration, margin (Reg T), insider trading = 1934 Act."
