       "type": "callout",
       "style": "note",
       "title": "Face-amount certificate — the rare one",
       "text": "An investor pays into an FAC and is promised a set dollar amount at a stated maturity date. Think of it as a debt-like savings contract issued by an investment company. It shows up only as a definitional item."
